// marsin_engine/secret.yaml — TITANIC shared pre-shared key (gitignored).
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for the AES-128-GCM key used by every component
// of the TITANIC ecosystem that talks Titanic Frame v2:
//
//   * marsin_engine itself (currently informational; engine doesn't sign
//     its own REST traffic — it lives behind a trusted LAN. Putting the
//     key here makes it the canonical place to look it up.)
//   * control_podium/companions/{bridge,client}_companion.py
//   * control_podium/companions/hil_*demo.py
//   * (future) CaptainPad iPad app, when it integrates with the radio
//     mesh — same file, same key.
//
// Companion apps look this file up RELATIVE TO THE REPO ROOT
// (../marsin_engine/secret.yaml). They REFUSE TO START if the file is
// missing — there is no implicit fallback to plaintext on the air.
//
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Bring-up
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  1. Copy this file to `secret.yaml` in this same directory:
//
//        cp marsin_engine/secret.yaml.example marsin_engine/secret.yaml
//
//  2. Edit `secret.yaml` and set `key:` (string) for dev or `key_hex:`
//     (32 hex chars) for production. Both formats are documented below.
//
//  3. Distribute the SAME file content to every other machine that runs
//     a companion — captain laptop, bridge laptop / Pi, future iPads.
//     USB stick or scp over a trusted LAN. NEVER send the key over the
//     radio. NEVER commit `secret.yaml` to git.
//
//  4. To rotate the key, generate a new one, push to every machine in
//     one operation, then restart everything. There is no in-band
//     rotation protocol — that's a deliberate post-burn item.
//
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Two key formats are accepted
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//   key:     "any-string"            ← derived: SHA-256(string)[:16]
//   key_hex: "32 hex chars exactly"  ← used directly as the AES-128-GCM key
//
// Use `key:` for hand-typed dev secrets ("SECRET", "burning-camp-2026", ...).
// Use `key_hex:` for production keys generated with:
//
//   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(16))"
//
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Threat model
// ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// Treat physical possession of any node (Heltec, iPad, Pi, laptop) as a
// key compromise — see docs/07_control_podium.md §3.6.1 for details.
// If a node is lost, rotate immediately.

# ─── Replace below with your real key, then save as secret.yaml ───

# Dev / bring-up: short string, derived via SHA-256.
key: "SECRET"

# Production alternative (uncomment + set; takes precedence over `key`):
# key_hex: "00112233445566778899aabbccddeeff"

# Format version. Lets us add a new cipher later without ambiguity.
# Currently the only supported value is 1 (AES-128-GCM, 12-byte nonce, 16-byte tag).
version: 1
